<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="git-addon-actions-git-staging">
  <title>Git Staging View Actions</title>
  <shortdesc>The following tables list actions that are unique to the Git Staging view, grouped by
    the area of the view where they appear.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>Git Staging view actions</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <refbody>
    <section id="section_git_staging_how_to_open">
      <title>How to Open Git Staging</title><p>To open the <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol> view,
        use one of the following:</p><ul>
        <li>Go to <menucascade>
            <uicontrol>Window</uicontrol>
            <uicontrol>Show View</uicontrol>
            <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol>
          </menucascade>.</li>
        <li>Go to <menucascade>
            <uicontrol>Tools</uicontrol>
            <uicontrol>Git Client</uicontrol>
          </menucascade>.</li>
        <li>Select <xref
            href="git-addon-actions-branches-history.dita#git-addon-actions-branches-history/action_show_staging"
              ><uicontrol>Show Staging</uicontrol></xref> from the <xref
            href="git-addon-git-menu.dita#git-addon-git-menu"><uicontrol>Git</uicontrol>
          menu</xref>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_file_area_actions">
      <title>File Area Actions</title><p>These actions are available in the context menu of the
          <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> and <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol> areas. See
          <xref
          href="git-addon-git-staging-view-interface.dita#git-addon-git-staging-view-interface/section_git_staging_file_areas"
        />.</p>
      <p><table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1" id="table_git_staging_file_area_actions">
          <title>Git Staging file area actions</title>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="2*"/>
            <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="5*"/>
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry>Action</entry>
                <entry>Description</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_open_in_compare_editor"
                      ><uicontrol>Open in Compare Editor</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Opens a comparison for the selected changed file so you can review the exact
                  edits before staging or committing it. Also triggered by double-clicking a file in
                  the <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_open"
                      ><uicontrol>Open</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Opens the selected file, folder, or submodule.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_stage"
                      ><uicontrol>Stage</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves the selected unstaged resource to the <uicontrol>Staged
                    files</uicontrol> area.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_discard"
                      ><uicontrol>Discard</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Discards a selected file's unstaged changes and replaces them with the last
                  committed version. Does not discard staged changes.</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table></p></section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_stage_controls">
      <title>Stage Controls</title><p>These controls appear between the <uicontrol>Unstaged
          files</uicontrol> and <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol> areas.</p><p><table frame="all"
          rowsep="1" colsep="1" id="table_git_staging_stage_controls">
          <title>Git Staging stage controls</title>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="2*"/>
            <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="5*"/>
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry>Action</entry>
                <entry>Description</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_stage_selected"
                      ><uicontrol>Stage Selected</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves the selected unstaged files to the <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol>
                  area.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_stage_all"
                      ><uicontrol>Stage All</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves all unstaged files to the <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol> area. Use
                  only when all current changes belong in the same commit.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_unstage_selected"
                      ><uicontrol>Unstage Selected</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves the selected staged files back to the <uicontrol>Unstaged
                    files</uicontrol> area without reverting local changes.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_unstage_all"
                      ><uicontrol>Unstage All</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves all staged files back to the <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area
                  without removing local changes.</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_commit_area_actions"><title>Commit Area Actions</title><p>These
        actions appear in the toolbar of the <uicontrol>Commit message</uicontrol> area. See <xref
          href="git-addon-committing.dita#git-addon-committing"/> for the commit
          workflow.</p><p><table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1"
          id="table_git_staging_commit_area_actions">
          <title>Git Staging commit area actions</title>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="2*"/>
            <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="5*"/>
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry>Action</entry>
                <entry>Description</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_commit"
                      ><uicontrol>Commit</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Saves the staged changes to the local repository with the message entered in
                  the <uicontrol>Commit message</uicontrol> area.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_generate_commit_message_ai"
                      ><uicontrol>Generate Commit Message Using AI</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Uses the <ph keyref="plugin-positron"/> assistant to generate a commit
                  message for the staged changes.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_choose_previous_comment"
                      ><uicontrol>Choose a Previously Used Comment</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Lets you reuse a previous commit message.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_auto_push_after_commit"
                      ><uicontrol>Automatically Push Changes to Remote
                  Branch</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Pushes the committed changes to the remote repository immediately after
                  committing.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_amend_last_commit"
                      ><uicontrol>Amend Last Commit</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Combines staged changes with the most recent commit or edits the last commit
                  message. Do not amend commits already pushed to a shared remote branch.</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table></p>
    </section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_conflict_actions"><title>Conflict Resolution
        Actions</title><p>These actions appear in the context menu of conflicted files in the
          <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area and in the conflict panel during in-progress
        operations. See <xref
          href="git-addon-resolve-file-conflicts.dita#git-addon-resolve-file-conflicts"
          />.</p><p><table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1" id="table_git_staging_conflict_actions">
          <title>Git Staging conflict resolution actions</title>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="2*"/>
            <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="5*"/>
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry>Action</entry>
                <entry>Description</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_resolve_using_mine"
                      ><uicontrol>Resolve Using Mine</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Resolves a conflicted file by keeping the local version and discarding the
                  incoming version.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_resolve_using_theirs"
                      ><uicontrol>Resolve Using Theirs</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Resolves a conflicted file by keeping the incoming version and discarding the
                  local version.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_resolve_with_ai"
                      ><uicontrol>Resolve with AI</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Uses the <ph keyref="plugin-positron"/> assistant to analyze a conflicted
                  file and propose a resolution. See <xref
                    href="git-addon-ai-assisted-conflict-resolution.dita#git-addon-ai-assisted-conflict-resolution"
                  />.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_mark_as_resolved"
                      ><uicontrol>Mark as Resolved</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Marks a conflicted file as resolved after you edit it and choose which
                  changes to keep.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_abort_operation"
                      ><uicontrol>Abort</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Stops the current in-progress operation and restores the repository to its
                  state before the operation started.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_restart_merge"
                      ><uicontrol>Restart Merge</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Restarts the current merge so you can resolve conflicts again from the
                  beginning.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_continue_rebase"
                      ><uicontrol>Continue Rebase</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Continues the current rebase after conflicts are resolved.</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>
      </p>
    </section>
  </refbody>
</reference>
